     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p><strong>Strictly necessary storage</strong></p>
+    <p>We use a session cookie to remember your reading list, and we store your privacy choices in your browser's local storage. This information stays on your device or is used only to provide the feature you requested. It is not used for analytics or advertising and does not require consent.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Your account</h2>
+    <p>To create an account we ask only for a <strong>username</strong> and a <strong>password</strong>. We do not ask for your real name, email address, phone number or date of birth. Your username can be any name you choose. Your credentials are sent over an encrypted connection (HTTPS) directly to our authentication service, which is hosted on Google Cloud. They are used solely to create your account and sign you in.</p>
+    <p>Requests to the authentication service are sent without cookies or a referring-page header. Sign-in and sign-up pages are never cached and are excluded from search engines. Your password is cleared from the page's memory after each attempt. These forms are excluded from click analytics.</p>
+    <p>You may request access to, correction of or deletion of your account at any time using the contact details in our <a href="imprint">Imprint</a>.</p>
+
+    <h2>5. Analytics (optional, off by default)</h2>
+    <p>With your consent only, we load an analytics script from our provider (<code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>). When you click a link or button, it sends the element type, its visible label and the time of the click. It does not record form inputs or account details, and it does not set identifiers. Until you opt in, the script is not downloaded at all.</p>
+
+    <h2>6. Advertising (optional, off by default)</h2>
+    <p>Ad slots are only requested from our advertising partner if you have given consent to advertising.</p>
+
+    <h2>7. Fonts and other third parties</h2>
+    <p>Our fonts are hosted on our own servers. Loading a page therefore does not send your IP address to a third-party font provider. We send only the origin of our site (never full page addresses) as a referrer to other websites. Through a Permissions Policy, we also disable browser features we don't need for ourselves and any embedded content. These include camera, microphone, geolocation and interest-based advertising topics.</p>
+
+    <h2>8. Your choices and browser signals</h2>
+    <p>On your first visit we ask whether you allow optional analytics and advertising. "Reject all" is always as easy as "Accept all". You can change or withdraw your consent at any time via <strong>Manage Privacy Preferences</strong> in the footer of every page.</p>
+    <p>If your browser sends a <strong>Global Privacy Control</strong> or <strong>Do Not Track</strong> signal, we treat it as a refusal: optional analytics and advertising stay off and we won't ask you.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
